SD Guthrie DMS Modules 

 

Creation of Dedicated SharePoint Site 

Description 
Creation of a dedicated SharePoint Online site specifically for the Document Management System (DMS). This site will serve as the centralized repository for document storage, approval workflow, metadata management, and access control. 

Scope Includes 

Site provisioning 

Site-level security groups (Admin, Approver, Uploader, Reader) 

Creation of required document libraries (e.g. Staging & Final) 

Basic site configuration 

Purpose 
To ensure security isolation, better governance, and easier permission management. 

 

Configure Metadata Columns 

Description 
Configuration of mandatory metadata fields in document libraries to ensure structured classification of documents. 

Examples of metadata fields 

Document Type 

Department / Business Unit 

Year / Period 

Document Date 

Project Name 

Confidentiality Level 

Vendor (if applicable) 

Purpose 
To ensure consistency, improve searchability, and support governance. 

 

Controlled Vocabulary (Term Store) 

Description 
Implementation of centralized managed metadata using SharePoint Term Store to enforce controlled dropdown values across document libraries. 

Scope Includes 

Creation of Term Groups 

Creation of Term Sets (e.g., Department, Document Type) 

Setup of dropdown-based selection 

Purpose 
To eliminate inconsistent data entry and ensure standardized classification. 

 

Enable Versioning & File Type Restrictions 

Description 
Configuration of document library settings to: 

Enable version control (optional) 

Restrict unsupported or risky file types (e.g., EXE, BAT) 

Allow only approved document formats 

Purpose 
To maintain document integrity and enhance security. 

 

Naming Convention Enforcement 

Description 
Implementation of standardized file naming structure based on defined business rules. Naming logic may be enforced through metadata. 

Example Format 
[Department]_[DocType]_[Project]_[Year].pdf 

Purpose 
To ensure uniform file naming and prevent inconsistencies. 

Staging Upload Mechanism 

Description 
Configuration of a staging document library where all uploads are first submitted for review before being approved and moved to the final repository. 

Scope Includes 

Separate staging library 

Mandatory metadata capture 

Controlled upload permissions 

Purpose 
To ensure only approved documents are stored in the final repository. 

 

Approval Workflow Automation 

Description 
Development of automated approval workflow using Power Automate to manage document review process. 

Process Flow 
Uploader → Approver → System action 

If Approved 

Document moved to final library 

Permissions updated (read-only) 

Notification sent 

If Rejected 

Notification sent to uploader 

Document removed or marked rejected 

Purpose 
To enforce governance and approval compliance. 

 

 

 

 

Escalation & Reminder Logic 

Description 
Configuration of automated reminder and escalation mechanism for pending approvals. 

Scope Includes 

Reminder email after defined number of days 

Optional escalation to secondary approver 

Email / Teams notifications 

Purpose 
To prevent approval delays and improve process efficiency. 

 

Duplicate & Conflict Detection 

Description 
Implementation of validation logic to detect: 

Duplicate filenames 

Metadata conflicts 

Existing document records 

System will: 

Prevent overwrite 

Allow versioning only  

Purpose 
To avoid data duplication and maintain document integrity. 

 

 

 

 

 

 

 

Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) 

Description 
Configuration of role-based permission model to control access and actions. 

Typical Roles 

Admin - Full control 

Approver - Review & approve 

Uploader - Upload to staging 

Reader - Read-only access 

Purpose 
To ensure security and department-level isolation. 

 

Audit Logging 

Description 
Enable audit logging to track user activities such as: 

Uploads 

Approvals 

Edits 

Deletions 

Access events 

Purpose 
To support compliance, governance, and audit requirements. 

 

Retention Policy Configuration 

Description 
Configuration of document retention rules based on organizational policy. 

Scope Includes 

Define retention duration 

Apply retention labels 

Prevent unauthorized deletion (if required) 

Purpose 
To ensure regulatory compliance and data lifecycle control. 

 

 Search & Retrieval 

Description 
Enable advanced document search functionality leveraging SharePoint indexing. 

Features 

Search by document title 

Search within document content (PDF/Office) 

Filter by metadata (Department, Year, Document Type, etc.) 

Pre-configured library views 

Purpose 
To allow efficient retrieval of documents. 

 